  "query_preview": "period of dry weather continues through the weekend and\nlikely through Thursday. A ridge extending north through the\nMississippi Valley will maintain a resemblance of an omega \nblock through the week. \n\nA weak trough with fast zonal flow will bring a cold front \nthrough the area on Monday. This front will have very little \nmoisture to work with but may be able to squeeze out some light\nrain showers through Monday morning before frontolysis takes\nover and washes the feature out over the Downeast region. Chance\nfor precip was increased with this forecast as the NBM likely\nwashed out the chance for such isolated/scattered showers, which\nreadily appear on individual CAMs runs. That said, with little\nmoisture to work with, only a hundredth or two of precipitation\nis expected at most, and generally dry conditions will continue\nwith no drought relief. Highs will be above normal on Sun and \nMon with temps dropping back into the 40s Tue and Wed behind the\nFROPA.",
